          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Fiber integration
            or
            %em push-forward
            is a process that sends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology"} generalized cohomology
            classes on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to B
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            to cohomology classes on the base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            of the bundle, by
            %em evaluating them on each fiber
            in some sense.
          %p
            This sense is such that if the cohomology in question is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            then fiber integration is ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            Composing pullback of cohomology classes with fiber integration yields the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#fiberwise_integration_of_ordinary_differential_forms Fiberwise integration of ordinary differential forms
          %p
            Consider a smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon T\to B
          %p
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            is a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*\colon\Omega^n(T)\to\Omega^{n-d}(B)
          %p
            defined as follows. Given
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega\in\Omega^n(T)
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-d)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*(\omega)
            is constructed as follows.
          %p
            The value of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*(\omega)
            at some collection of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-d)
            tangent vector fields
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_{n-d}
            is computed as follows.
          %p
            First, lift each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i
            to a section of the quotient bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(T)/T(f)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f)
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                relative tangent bundle
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/relative+tangent+bundle"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_i
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(T)
            in some arbitrary way. Substitute the resulting vector fields on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            into the differential
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            to each of the fibers of the map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon T\to B
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_i
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*(\omega)
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_{n-d}
          %p See Greub, Halperin, and Vanstone, Volume I, Section VII.7.12.
          %h3#in_generalized_cohomology_via_pontryaginthom_collapse_maps In generalized cohomology via Pontryagin-Thom collapse maps
          %h4#along_maps_of_manifolds Along maps of manifolds
          %p
            Here is the rough outline of the construction via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+collapse+maps"} Pontryagin-Thom collapse maps
          %p The basic strategy is this:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                start with a map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to B
            %li
              %p
                make
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                bigger without changing its homotopy type such that the map from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                becomes an
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
            %li
              %p
                choose an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation
                structure that makes the cohomology of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                equivalent to that of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Th
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th(E)
                (the
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
            %li
              %p
                compose the Thom isomorphism with the pullback along
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi Th
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to Th(E)
                to get an “Umkehr” map from cohomology of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                to cohomology of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p Now in detail.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : E \to B
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            of smooth compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            with typical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney+embedding+theorem"} Whitney embedding theorem
            one can choose an embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:E \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^n
            for some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (p,e) : E \hookrightarrow B \times \mathbb{R}^n
                  \\,.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{(p,e)} (E)
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            relative to this embedding. It is a rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mi dim
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n- dim F
            bundle over the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \times \mathbb{R}^n
          %p
            Fix a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhood"} tubular neighbourhood
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \times \mathbb{R}^n
            and identify it with the total space of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{(p,e)}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∖
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \times \mathbb{R}^n \setminus N_{(p,e)}(E)
            to a point gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{(p,e)}(E)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Th
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \times \mathbb{R}^n
                  \\to
                  B \times \mathbb{R}^n / (B \times \mathbb{R}^n - N_{(p,e)}(E))
                  \\simeq
                  Th(N_{(p,e)}(E))
          %p
            factors through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B \times \mathbb{R}^n)^*
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \times \mathbb{R}^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B \times \mathbb{R}^n)^*\cong \Sigma^n B_+
            (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "one-point+compactification#MonoidalFunctoriality"} here
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_+
            (or, equivalently, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            with the
            = succeed "-sphere:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mo +
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^n B_+= S^n \wedge B_+
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo +
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi τ
                  %mi Th
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \times \mathbb{R}^n \to \Sigma^n B_+ \stackrel{\tau}{\to} Th(N_{(p,e)}(E))
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+collapse+map"} Pontrjagin-Thom collapse map
          %p
            Explicitly, as sets we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo +
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^n B_+ \simeq B \times \mathbb{R}^n \cup \{\infty\}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th(N_{(e,p)}(E)) = N_{(e,p)} \cup \{\infty\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset \Sigma^n B_+
            a tubular neighbourhood of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : U \to N_{(e,p)}(E)
            an isomorphism, the map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo +
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                  %mi Th
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau : \Sigma^n B_+ \stackrel{}{\to} Th(N_{(p,e)}(E))
          %p is defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi U
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn ∞
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi otherwise
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau : x \mapsto
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\phi(x) &amp; | &amp; x \in U
                  \\\
                  \\infty &amp; | &amp; otherwise
                  }
                  \\right.
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            be some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Th
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th(N_{(p,e)}(E))
            has an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+isomorphism"} suspension isomorphism
            the pullback along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            produces a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
